{
  "slug": "sensei",
  "name": "Sensei",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Sensei is a Claude Code plugin that turns any project into a guided learning environment. It installs a persistent AI mentor — selectable between Master Splinter and Gandalf — that teaches through the Socratic method rather than serving direct answers.\nKey behaviors:  Code gate — refuses to give code unless the student uses a character-specific safeword or demo trigger\n- Session lifecycle — /dojo-open sets a micro-goal, /pizza-time closes the session  and updates progress tracking\n- Spaced repetition — tracks concepts introduced, practiced, and mastered across sessions\n- Character integrity — hooks enforce voice and teaching stance across every message, preventing drift",
  "longDescription": "Ships **14 skills** and **1 hook**.\n\n- **Skills** (14): `challenge-me` (Generate a project-relevant exercise with acceptance criteria), `commands` (Show available commands and their triggers), `dojo-open` (Open a teaching session with briefing and skill pulse), `notecards` (Quiz the student using spaced repetition from the Concept Index), `pizza-time` (Close the session and update progress tracking files), `progress-report` (Visual summary of mastery levels and learning progress), `reset` (Re-establish Sensei teaching mode if character voice or Socratic discipline has drifted), `sensei-check` (Validate Sensei setup — confirms CONFIG.md, character, safeword, ROADMAP.md, and PROGRESS.md are present), and 6 more\n- **Hooks** (1): `hooks.json`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install sensei@claude-community` from `jreynolds-dev/sensei`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 14,
    "hook": 1
  },
  "sourceType": "community",
